BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
UID:TU2025222010
DTSTAMP:20260704T160315Z
SUMMARY:Jewish without Apology: A Conversation with Sarah Hurwitz
DESCRIPTION:**Seth Goodchild Memorial Lecture**  \nReception immediately fo
 llowing  \n  \nEvent is at capacity. To be added to the waiting list\, con
 tact: Email Aviva Arad\, aarad@shomrei.org  \n  \n**LIVESTREAM  \nThis eve
 nt will be livestreamed but NOT recorded. To watch remotely\, you must tun
 e in at the time of the event:  http://shomrei.org/live: https://shomrei.o
 rg/live**  \n  \n**About the Program**  \nAward-winning author Sarah Hurwi
 tz joins Rabbi Julie Roth for a candid conversation about rediscovering Ju
 daism as an adult and why its intellectual depth and moral clarity feel st
 rikingly relevant to modern life. From finding meaning in a chaotic world 
 to standing tall against rising antisemitism\, Sarah explores why embracin
 g Jewish wisdom isn’t just about honoring the past -- it’s about sanct
 ifying the present and elevating our shared humanity.   \n  \n**Free Babys
 itting Available**  \nEmail Aviva Arad\, aarad@shomrei.org  \n  \n**\\*Add
 itional parking is available next door at 73 &amp\; 77 Park Street.**  \n 
  \n**In Loving Memory of Seth Goodchild**   \nSeth Goodchild was inspired 
 by his family to convert to Judaism at the end of his life. To honor his l
 egacy and share his love of Judaism\, his friends and family sponsored thi
 s lecture and a class on exploring Judaism.\n\n
LOCATION:Sanctuary\, Livestream
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
