BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
UID:TU2065829319
DTSTAMP:20260704T160315Z
SUMMARY:Yom HahShoah Program: After the Holocaust: Family History\, Memory\
 , and Identity 
DESCRIPTION:**Community Program:**   \n7:15PM: Light Meal - Social Hall  \n
 7:40PM - 9:00PM: Program - Sanctuary   \n  \n**RSVP:** https://shomrei.eas
 yshul.com/events/69c290772fc4cd002701d871  \n**After the Holocaust:** **Fa
 mily History\, Memory\, and Identity**  \nIn the aftermath of World War II
 \, Jewish survivors in Displaced Persons (DP) camps rebuilt their lives wi
 th remarkable resilience\, creating families and ushering in an unpreceden
 ted baby boom. At the same time\, family memory—preserved through storie
 s\, documents\, and traditions—became a powerful means of reconstructing
  identity after profound loss. In this lecture\, Dr. Serafima Velkovich ex
 plores how family history research and personal narratives intersect with 
 the history of DP camps and demonstrates how individuals can uncover trace
 s of former DP babies within their own family histories.  \n  \n*Join a co
 nversation with Dr. Sera Velkovich of Yad Vashem and Shirley Grill of Shom
 rei Emunah as they explore the resilience\, and rebuilding of lives in the
  aftermath of the Shoah.*\n\n  \n  \nKey fob required for building entry. 
  \n**Questions?**  \nContact the Shomrei Office  \noffice@shomrei.org  \n(
 973) 746-5031\n\n
LOCATION:Sanctuary\, Social Hall
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
